    "description": "Mineral Identification Collection Kit\nGeological Specimen Study Set\n8 Natural Mineral Samples in Display Box\n8\" x 6\" x 2\"\nNumbered Collection\nThis professional mineral identification kit is an essential resource for geological education and scientific observation. The collection consists of eight distinct natural mineral specimens, including recognizable samples such as crystalline quartz, pink feldspar, and metallic pyrite. Each sample is individually numbered, allowing for systematic classification and study of physical properties such as luster, crystal habit, and cleavage.\nFeatures 8 high-quality natural specimens housed in a 9-compartment white plastic organizer\nHoused in a durable red textured storage case with a protective foam-lined interior lid\nProvides a hands-on learning experience for students, hobbyists, and amateur geologists\nCondition:\nVery good pre-owned condition. The kit contains 8 specimens total, leaving one slot in the tray currently vacant. The minerals are well-preserved and stable. The storage box remains structurally sound with light age-appropriate wear to the exterior finish.\nPlease Note:\nThis is a pre-owned item being sold\nas-is\n. We do our best to describe items accurately and include research where possible, but we are not experts in every category. Please note that if the title or description states \"Tested\" that we only test to make sure the unit \"\nPOWERS ON\"\n.\nNo further testing takes place unless stated otherwise and items are considered untested.\nPlease remember all items are used and are sold as is, no refunds.If you have questions, please contact us before bidding.\nFor all vintage clothing, please research sizing before placing a bid.\nItems from different time periods may have measurements that differ from today’s standard sizing.\nCustomer Service:\nReach us via the “Contact Us” link above or by calling\n(540) 361-6550\n. Messages are handled Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:00 PM ET, and we strive to respond within 48 hours.",
