    "description": "Gemstones of the World\nEducational Mineral Specimen Display Card\n12 Polished Tumbled Stones, Cardstock Backing\nThis educational geological display card features twelve polished gemstone and mineral specimens mounted to an illustrated global map backing. Study cards of this type were popular educational aids, tourist souvenirs, and lapidary collector reference pieces. Each tumbled specimen is clearly identified by stone variety along with its noted geographic source.\nIncludes 12 mounted specimens: Aventurine, Ruby Cullet, Lace Agate, Apache Tear, Jasper, Fluorite, Amethyst, Turquesite, Tigereye, Peridot, Petrified Wood, and Rose Quartz\nPrinted cream cardstock backer featuring a red world map graphic and bold specimen text\nTumbled and polished smooth stone surfaces with glossy finishes\nMeasures approximately 5 inches by 3 inches\nCondition:\nAll 12 stone specimens remain intact and affixed to the card. The cardstock backing shows pronounced creasing, including a vertical crease down the center, surface wrinkles, corner softening, and vintage age toning. Adhesive residue is visible around stone mounts as originally applied.\nThank you for all of your support!",
